### GET Public endpoint - no login required
GET http://localhost:8080/

### GET Obtain CSRF token to add to headers for other requests
### Request a CSRF token before state-changing requests (POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, and logout).
### Only repeat this request if you do not already have a valid XSRF-TOKEN or the request returns 403 due to CSRF.
GET http://localhost:8080/csrf

### POST Register New User - no login required
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: t0709uRWRRQkIxcRK03R4hyOJ9wk4_ybAbO938neIbJRaIvu1HnMx4FhJ3EJEiEkGmDl1S67CuUS1ci2Ytbf7Py_GYYyDr6K

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### POST Login with already existing admin
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
X-XSRF-TOKEN: t0709uRWRRQkIxcRK03R4hyOJ9wk4_ybAbO938neIbJRaIvu1HnMx4FhJ3EJEiEkGmDl1S67CuUS1ci2Ytbf7Py_GYYyDr6K

email=admin@example.com&password=Password

### POST Login with registered user
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
X-XSRF-TOKEN: t0709uRWRRQkIxcRK03R4hyOJ9wk4_ybAbO938neIbJRaIvu1HnMx4FhJ3EJEiEkGmDl1S67CuUS1ci2Ytbf7Py_GYYyDr6K

email=user@example.com&password=password123

### USER ENDPOINT - USER + ADMIN - Login Required
GET http://localhost:8080/api/user

